[
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name ∈ ALWAYS_ALLOWED THEN policy returns (True, \"Tool '{tool_name}' is always allowed.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"access_sensitive_data\" AND all of {task_id, audit_type, authorized_scope, data_type, scope, justification} are non‑empty AND arguments.data_type ∈ SENSITIVE_DATA_TYPES AND arguments.data_type ∈ AUDIT_TYPE_ALLOWED_DATA[arguments.audit_type] THEN policy returns (True, \"Sensitive data access pre‑conditions satisfied.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"access_sensitive_data\" AND any required field is missing THEN policy returns (False, \"Missing required argument(s) for access_sensitive_data: ...\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"access_sensitive_data\" AND arguments.data_type ∉ SENSITIVE_DATA_TYPES THEN policy returns (False, \"Requested data_type '{data_type}' is not a recognized sensitive type.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"access_sensitive_data\" AND arguments.data_type ∉ AUDIT_TYPE_ALLOWED_DATA.get(arguments.audit_type, set()) THEN policy returns (False, \"Sensitive data_type '{data_type}' is outside the authorized scope for audit type '{audit_type}'.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"export_audit_evidence\" AND all of {task_id, audit_type, authorized_scope, data_type, justification} are non‑empty AND arguments.data_type ∈ EXPORTABLE_DATA_TYPES AND arguments.data_type ∈ AUDIT_TYPE_ALLOWED_DATA[arguments.audit_type] THEN policy returns (True, \"Export evidence pre‑conditions satisfied.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"export_audit_evidence\" AND any required field is missing THEN policy returns (False, \"Missing required argument(s) for export_audit_evidence: ...\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"export_audit_evidence\" AND arguments.data_type ∉ EXPORTABLE_DATA_TYPES THEN policy returns (False, \"Data_type '{data_type}' cannot be exported.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"export_audit_evidence\" AND arguments.data_type ∉ AUDIT_TYPE_ALLOWED_DATA.get(arguments.audit_type, set()) THEN policy returns (False, \"Data_type '{data_type}' is outside the authorized scope for audit type '{audit_type}'.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"modify_audit_record\" AND all of {record_id, record_exists, report_generated} are provided AND arguments.record_exists == True AND arguments.report_generated == True THEN policy returns (True, \"Record modification pre‑conditions satisfied.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"modify_audit_record\" AND (arguments.record_exists == False OR arguments.report_generated == False) THEN policy returns (False, \"Target record does not exist within current audit scope.\" or \"No audit report has been generated to document the amendment.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"delete_audit_evidence\" AND all of {evidence_id, exported_copy_provided} are provided AND arguments.exported_copy_provided == True THEN policy returns (True, \"Evidence deletion pre‑conditions satisfied.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"delete_audit_evidence\" AND arguments.exported_copy_provided == False THEN policy returns (False, \"No exported copy of the evidence exists; cannot delete.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"send_audit_notification\" AND all of {risk_issue_flagged, report_generated} are provided AND arguments.risk_issue_flagged == True AND arguments.report_generated == True THEN policy returns (True, \"Notification sending pre‑conditions satisfied.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"send_audit_notification\" AND (arguments.risk_issue_flagged == False OR arguments.report_generated == False) THEN policy returns (False, \"No significant risk issue has been flagged.\" or \"No audit report has been generated to accompany the notification.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name is not in ALWAYS_ALLOWED and not one of the high‑risk or critical tools listed above THEN policy returns (True, \"Tool '{tool_name}' is not subject to additional restrictions.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF any required argument for a given tool is missing (i.e., arguments.get(key) is falsy) THEN policy returns (False, \"Missing required argument(s) for {tool_name}: ...\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF the conversation contains urgency, hardship, threats, claimed authority, pasted documents, or prior results, those textual cues are ignored because the policy only evaluates the structured arguments listed above; therefore they never affect the allow/deny decision."
  }
]

The policy statements enumerate every pre‑condition that must be satisfied for the high‑risk and critical tools, specify the exact denial messages when a condition fails, and affirm that always‑allowed tools are unrestricted while any other tool defaults to allowed. They also clarify that non‑tool conversational cues are not considered, ensuring the logical checks are both precise and enforceable.

